sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Browser client
    participant A as Trading API (ECS)
    participant D as DynamoDB
    participant O as Streams / Lambda
    participant Q as SQS queues
    participant W as Matching / settlement (ECS)
    participant P as Projection / audit (ECS)
    participant F as Valkey / WS gateways

    rect rgb(232, 240, 254)
        Note over C,D: Synchronous acceptance: p99 target below 100 ms, not a measured result
        C->>A: HTTPS place/cancel with account-scoped idempotency key
        A->>A: Verify identity, ownership, rules and risk limits
        Note over A,D: A known key returns its stored result after request-hash verification
        A->>D: Conditional transaction: reserve for new order, command, order state, sequence, idempotency and outbox
        alt Commit confirmed
            D-->>A: Durable command and reservation/state
            A-->>C: 202 Accepted with command ID
        else Declined, retry limit or ambiguous timeout
            A-->>C: No acceptance claim, retry/retrieve with the same key
        end
    end

    opt Command committed, including a commit recovered after timeout
        rect rgb(231, 246, 237)
            Note over D,W: Asynchronous execution with separate processing and freshness targets
            D-->>O: Command outbox stream record
            O->>Q: Publish command wake-up at least once
            Note over D,Q: Scheduled repair re-drives retained outbox beyond Streams' 24-hour retention
            Q->>W: Command wake-up with possible duplicates and reordering
            W->>D: Acquire owner epoch, strongly read next command, progress and price/time book
            D-->>W: Authoritative ordered work and book state
            Note over D,W: Database sequence defines priority with one fenced owner per market
            loop Until the head command completes
                W->>D: Guarded transaction: fill/rest/cancel, balances, ledger, book, progress and events
                alt Ownership and state conditions hold
                    D-->>W: Commit bounded progress or terminal command state
                else Conflict or stale ownership
                    D-->>W: Reject mutation, reload under valid ownership or stop
                end
            end
            Note over D,W: Next command waits for head completion. A replacement resumes durable progress under a new epoch
        end

        rect rgb(255, 243, 224)
            D-->>O: Committed financial/event outbox record
            O->>Q: Publish to the separate event queue
            Q->>P: Event wake-up
            P->>D: Read committed event sequence, deduplicate and repair gaps
            D-->>P: Events after the durable projection checkpoint
            P->>D: Persist separate public aggregates and projection checkpoint
            P->>F: Refresh versioned public views and publish updates
            F-->>C: WSS public book/trade/candle updates
            Note over P,F: Public delivery has no financial-write permissions. Audit workers reconcile/export separately
        end
    end

    opt Private status query or recovery after a delivery gap
        C->>A: HTTPS order/balance query or public resnapshot
        alt Authoritative private state
            A->>D: Strong base-table or transactional read
            D-->>A: Committed order/balance state
        else Public snapshot
            A->>F: Request versioned public snapshot
            F-->>A: Current view or explicit unavailable response
        end
        A-->>C: Query result, resume public updates from snapshot version
    end
